WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.920
we're doing sunscreen reviews!

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.640
yay!

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.200
it's Michelle of lab muffin&nbsp;
beauty science chemistry PhD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.480
cosmetic chemist and sunscreen connoisseur

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.840
today I'm talking about a bunch of&nbsp;
international sunscreens I've tried recently

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.200
all of these are quite popular on social media

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.400
there's two from haruharu this video's sponsor

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.800
the rest are sunscreens that I picked up when I&nbsp;
was in the US a little while back for open sauce

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.160
I've been dying to try out some of these for years

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.840
and I know that a lot of us sunscreen nerds&nbsp;
are not really that into US sunscreens

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.360
but honestly it didn't go that badly

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.600
not as badly as I expected anyway

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.520
I'm going to start with the haruharu wonder&nbsp;
black rice moisture airfit daily sunscreen

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.920
this is a Korean chemical sunscreen&nbsp;
with a different formula from a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.240
of the ones that are really popular at the moment

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.760
I think most people have heard about&nbsp;
this like family of Korean chemical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.600
sunscreens that are sort of&nbsp;
like variations on a theme

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.360
they use this blend of filters

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.720
they each have slightly different skincare&nbsp;
ingredients and textures and they are some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.760
of my favorite sunscreens of all time

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.520
but some people have told me that&nbsp;
they don't really like these formulas

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.600
they can have white cast on darker skin&nbsp;
probably because of that mbbt filter

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.960
it is a chemical or organic sunscreen but it is&nbsp;
in particles so it scatters more visible light

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.440
some people don't like the texture and&nbsp;
some people just find them kind of boring

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.080
so this haruharu sunscreen is an&nbsp;
alternative chemical sunscreen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.520
formula which uses these different filters

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.040
and you will notice there is no mbbt there

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.160
so this one has zero white cast&nbsp;
on me and I've seen reviews from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.480
people with darker skin saying it&nbsp;
has no white cast on them as well

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.880
it's also made by Kolmar which is the big Korean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.920
sunscreen manufacturer that makes a lot&nbsp;
of the really popular Korean sunscreens

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.640
I'd say this is on the more moisturizing and&nbsp;
creamy end of Korean chemical sunscreens but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.600
it is still really lightweight with&nbsp;
a creme gel moisturizer consistency

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.960
it applies really smoothly&nbsp;
and feels hydrating without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.160
being greasy and it leaves a slightly&nbsp;
tacky moisturized feeling on your skin

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.320
I think a lot of people underestimate&nbsp;
the importance of the inactives in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.680
a product when it comes to the texture&nbsp;
and the overall experience of sunscreen

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.040
so I'm going to talk a little bit more&nbsp;
about them and this is actually like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.720
one of the few times I think reading the&nbsp;
ingredients list can be kind of helpful

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.120
to get the cream gel consistency which is&nbsp;
popular in so many Asian skincare products

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.040
not just with sunscreens but&nbsp;
also with like moisturizers

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.080
formulas usually use a polymeric emulsifier&nbsp;

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:19.640
that means it will hold the oily and watery&nbsp;
parts of a product together without needing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.440
as much of those traditional emulsifiers&nbsp;
which can feel a bit thick and heavy&nbsp;

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.880
closer to the top of the ingredients list
for this is polyglyceryl-3 distearate&nbsp;

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.840
this goes on a little bit shiny but it sinks in&nbsp;
pretty quickly and it glides on just so smoothly&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.120
there's no fragrance and it doesn't pill on&nbsp;
me and it sits really nicely under my makeup&nbsp;

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.000
in terms of other skincare actives this&nbsp;
has ceramides as well as niacinamide and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.320
adenosine and that's what makes this&nbsp;
a triple functional cosmetic in Korea&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.760
in other words as well as being an SPF&nbsp;
is also brightening and anti-wrinkle

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.560
Haruharu also has this other sunscreen which is&nbsp;
the black rice pure mineral relief daily sunscreen&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:02.080
this is another fragrance free sunscreen and it&nbsp;
mostly uses zinc oxide as well as an SPF booster&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.440
this goes on with a bit of white cast&nbsp;
which is what you expect from a zinc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.640
oxide sunscreen but it dries down&nbsp;
to only a tiny amount of white cast&nbsp;

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.800
it is as good as I've tried with&nbsp;
any untinted zinc oxide sunscreen&nbsp;

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.760
the finish is not very greasy it's more of&nbsp;
like a hydrated finish and it is slightly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.440
slide-y so you can blend out any white streaks&nbsp;
pretty easily after it's mostly dried down&nbsp;

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.840
again this has a cream gel consistency&nbsp;
and it uses a polymeric emulsifier&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.440
this one is a little bit worse&nbsp;
just in terms of like reading it&nbsp;

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.640
it's polyglyceryl-3&nbsp;
polydimethylsiloxyethyl dimethicone&nbsp;

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:40.120
I personally tend not to prefer mineral sunscreens&nbsp;
but this is one of my favorite formulas so far&nbsp;

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.880
again it's from Kolmar and I just feel&nbsp;
like they really know how to make good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:48.080
sunscreens that people enjoy using
it's also got niacinamide hyaluronic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.400
acid and I think that's what contributes to&nbsp;
this being not too drying and not too greasy&nbsp;

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.400
it is just hydrating which is pretty&nbsp;
rare with mineral sunscreens on my skin

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.200
I always love a good pump&nbsp;
container with my sunscreens&nbsp;

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.920
I find them really nice and easy&nbsp;
to dispense and you can easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:07.360
work out how many pumps you need to use
I personally have this problem and maybe you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:13.600
do too I kind of accidentally just start using&nbsp;
less and less sunscreen over time and I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.160
necessarily notice and every once in a while I'll&nbsp;
have to recalibrate how much sunscreen I'm using&nbsp;

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.120
so pumps are really good for that&nbsp;
because then you can just say&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.800
I will always put on X number of pumps which I've&nbsp;
measured out once and never have to measure again&nbsp;

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.840
for my face these ones I would need three pumps&nbsp;
and it would be three to six pumps probably for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.160
most people depending on the size of your face
and it also depends on how much of your hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:40.160
you use to apply because that will also count&nbsp;
as extra surface area and it can be quite a lot&nbsp;

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.520
both of these are available from the official&nbsp;
Amazon page and the links are in the description

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:48.680
I picked up a whole bunch of popular US&nbsp;
sunscreens to try and this is really not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.200
meant to be like a comparison video&nbsp;
because it would be pretty unfair to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.520
compare US sunscreens with Korean sunscreens
they have different filters and very different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.680
regulations so really this is like a&nbsp;
good opportunity for me to get a bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:06.080
of sunscreen reviews out there because I have&nbsp;
